# Benchmark workloads of `qvto bench` (DESIGN §7.1). Case-file format (crates/qvto-testkit/README.md)
# plus `bench <key> <value>` lines (crates/qvto-cli/src/bench.rs): group, series (runs on the same,
# changing models), rounds, runs. Paths are relative to the repository root; models under
# target/qvto-bench/gen are generated by `qvto bench gen` (done automatically): SimpleUML and
# Ecore models scaled 1x/10x/100x, the corpus PCM models with (scale - 1) * k more resource
# containers, assembly and allocation contexts.

# B2: SimuLizar reconfiguration rules (measurement above the thresholds: the rules act)

case b2_lb_scaleUp_x1
kind bench
qvto target/qvto-bench/gen/pcm/loadbalancer-x1/scaleUp.qvto
in target/qvto-bench/gen/pcm/loadbalancer-x1/prm-high.xmi
in target/qvto-bench/gen/pcm/loadbalancer-x1/loadbalancer_on_iaas.allocation
conf target/pcm/pcm.conf
imports folder
bench group B2
end

case b2_lb_scaleIn_x1
kind bench
qvto target/qvto-bench/gen/pcm/loadbalancer-x1/scaleIn.qvto
in target/qvto-bench/gen/pcm/loadbalancer-x1/prm-high.xmi
in target/qvto-bench/gen/pcm/loadbalancer-x1/loadbalancer_on_iaas.allocation
conf target/pcm/pcm.conf
imports folder
bench group B2
end

